          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            A 10,000 watt generator is an 8,000 to 9,000 running-watt machine, and that is enough for a well pump, a furnace, a refrigerator and freezer, and one big 240V appliance at a time. Central air needs a soft starter. Buy for the running watts and the 50-amp outlet, not the peak number on the box.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most buyers the Champion 201417 is the one to get. Choose the DuroMax XP11000iH if you will run mostly on propane, and the Generac GP8000E only if a 30-amp, gasoline-only setup covers what you need.
